ASCILINE·Rust — NOTICE
======================

This project is a from-scratch Rust re-implementation of the backend engine of
ASCILINE (https://github.com/YusufB5/ASCILINE), Copyright (c) 2026 YusufB5,
released under the MIT License (with Anti-Advertisement Restriction), a copy of
which is in LICENSE.

The following files in web/ are copied unmodified from the original project and
remain under its license:

  web/index.html   — web player UI
  web/app.js       — frontend WebSocket client + canvas render loop
  web/style.css    — player styling
  web/codec.js     — shared adaptive-codec decoder (browser/Node)

They are served by the Rust server (asciline-server) so that the original
browser client works against the Rust backend unchanged.

  experiments/vendor/codec.py — the original adaptive + tag-4 profile encoder
  (commit 7003c2f), copied unmodified

It is used only to regenerate the committed differential test vectors
(experiments/vectors_python.bin, vectors_profile_py.bin) with the exact
encoder the Rust port is verified bit-exact against; pinning it keeps those
vectors reproducible in CI without a checkout of the upstream repo.

The wire protocol (INIT text handshake, binary frame format
[4-byte frame index BE][1-byte codec tag][payload], codec tags 0-3, and the .ascf
v2 "ASC2" container) is re-implemented from the original project's public
protocol, with the codec verified bit-exact against the original encoder and
decoder by the differential tests in experiments/ and tests/.
